# ReShade.fxh GetLinearizedDepth with reversed depth and the far plane F as a
# compile-time input (the preprocessor definition RESHADE_DEPTH_LINEARIZATION_FAR_PLANE,
# default 1000, realistic range 100..10000). The search runs at F = 1000, then the
# candidate's constants are generalized into expressions of F (1 / (F - 1),
# F / (F - 1)^2) and verified over the whole range. The original's own rounding error
# (4.2e-4 at F = 10000) exceeds the general rel 1e-6 budget; the rewrite passes by the
# accuracy rule (1.5e-7 vs exact math).
# expect: mad(rcp(t + rcp(F - 1.0)), F / ((F - 1.0) * (F - 1.0)), rcp(1.0 - F))
input t : float in [0, 1] grid 16777215
input F : const float in [100, 10000] = 1000
output r = (1.0 - t) / (F - (1.0 - t) * (F - 1.0))
budget r : rel 1e-6
